     PRECISION DISCIPLINE.  A first pass ran beta(a=1) in the LARGER box
     (deg<=8, ht<=1e10) at dps=100 / tol=1e-60 and reported a degree-6 relation
     with coefficients ~4.4e9.  That is a SPURIOUS hit: PSLQ on n numbers with
     height-10^H coefficients needs working precision comfortably above n*H
     digits, and 9 numbers x 10 digits = 90 > the 60 digits of tolerance used.
     The controls above were run in the SMALLER box, so they did not cover it.
     Re-run below at dps=300 / tol=1e-200, WITH the controls re-run in the SAME
     box -- which is the only way the result means anything.
     beta(a=1) to 200 digits =
